        "8 of the 9 domains (all but security_resolution, which predates this packet) are applied as one 16-file (8 ingest + 8 entitlement) packet through the staging-only netquity_serving_writer_staging role; the packet and its 4 companion domain-CHECK-constraint migrations are additive-only, confirmed by an explicit destructive-statement scan",
        "netquity_serving_writer_staging can write entitlement/serving rows through 4 role-targeted RLS policies but cannot run DDL; the 4 domain migrations stay admin-channel only",
        "scripts/apply-netquity-staging-promotions.mjs defaults to a dry-run plan; applying the packet requires an explicit --execute --use-keychain invocation",
        "apps/worker/src/authenticated-netquity-web-resolver.ts (AuthenticatedNetquityResolver on the private AIPHABEE_API binding) is not public-HTTP-exposed and authorizes every call against workspace/data entitlement before touching the Hyperdrive binding",
        "every resolver method returns only the latest released serving snapshot, exact entity_id lookups only, capped at 1 row per domain call",
        "authorization defaults to deny (default_rights_status: default_deny); each domain carries its own rights_policy_version and requested-field allowlist",
        "the 9 apps/web/src/lib/api/*.server.ts resolvers (including derived-metrics.server.ts) backing the workbench panels are live; DerivedPanel's profitability and valuation (P/E and other market-cap-dependent) metrics are computed live by packages/workbench's createLiveDerivedMetrics from the resolveDerivedMetrics RPC, which conjuncts the financial_facts and quote_snapshot Web entitlement gates (both required, no separate derived-metrics dataset or rights row) and independently degrades either dataset's absence to a graded blocked_reason per metric (financial_facts_not_found, quote_unavailable, shares_outstanding_unavailable, missing_input, quality_hold, zero/negative_denominator) rather than a synthesized value",
